Newspeak3
'Test'
(* newspeak-spec.pdf 5.1.3: nil "responds to almost all messages with a
   messageNotUnderstood error. The exceptions are isNil, which answers true
   and methods inherited from class Value." So isNil is the one selector
   5.1.3 obliges nil to answer, and the answer it fixes is true.

   Only nil is probed here. 5.1.3 lists isNil as an exception to nil's own
   messageNotUnderstood behaviour rather than as a method of Object, and
   isNil appears nowhere else in the specification, so what a non-nil
   receiver answers is not a rule this file may record. *)
class Spec513NilIsNil usingPlatform: p = Object new (| t = p transcript. |) (
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        t show: nil isNil printString; newLine.
    )
) : ()
